      "message": "Using FP_BITS will not work when float type is used.\n\nThe formula to encode is:\n(799.797 * (crgb_data[0]* 0.009) +\n\t    crgb_data[1]* 0.056) +\n\t    crgb_data[2]* 2.735) +\n\t    crgb_data[3]* -1.903)) * 1000 / (integration_time_us*cur_gain);\n\nSo it should look like:\n\nxyz_data[1] \u003d FP_TO_INT(fp_div(fp_mul(FLOAT_TO_FP(799.797),\n                     (fp_mul(INT_TO_FP(crgb_data[0]), FLOAT_TO_FP(0.009)) +\n                      fp_mul(INT_TO_FP(crgb_data[1]), FLOAT_TO_FP(0.056)) +\n                      fp_mul(INT_TO_FP(crgb_data[2]), FLOAT_TO_FP(2.735)) +\n                      fp_mul(INT_TO_FP(crgb_data[3]), FLOAT_TO_FP(-1.903))),\n                      INT_TO_FP(integration_time_us * cur_gain / 1000ULL))",
